   "source": [
    "### Data Validation Findings\n",
    "\n",
    "- There are no missing values present since all of the 100 rows contain complete information (10 thresholds of alert x 10 levels of manpower).\n",
    "- The detection rate varies between 7% and 94.5% while the cost savings vary between \$0 and \$15,768 of daily expenses.\n",
    "- A correlation coefficient of -0.24 indicates a weak correlation between detection rate and cost savings; alert threshold exerts more influence on detection than staffing does.\n",
    "- The charts show that the peak detection is detected at the middle thresholds (from 30 to 50), and the detection is reduced at high thresholds as the cost of manpower is reduced gradually with the increase of manpower.\n",
    "- The data coincides with the proposal: more professionals mean higher expenses and the threshold determines the amount of suspected attacks."
   ]
